--
-- Description
-- -----------
-- This tests the maximum single packet limit of the TX packet buffer.
-- 
-- This tests with a programmed AHB burst length of 4-beats using a 4K RAM.
--
--
--      NOTE: MAX FRAME SIZES(BYTES) ARE AS FOLLOWS:-
--
--        gem_tx_pbuf_addr  | Use HALF | 4-BEAT | 8-BEAT | 16-BEAT
--                          | of SRAM? |        |        |
--       ----------------------------------------------------------
--         10 (32bit)       |  YES     |  2016  |  1984  |  1920
--         10 (32bit)       |  NO      |  4064  |  4032  |  3968
--         10 (64bit)       |  YES     |  4035  |  3972  |  3844
--         10 (64bit)       |  NO      |  8132  |  8068  |  7940
--
--
-- 
-- Functional Coverage
-- -------------------
-- * Checks TX packet buffer full for 4-beat bursts
-- * Checks TX packet buffer overflow handling for 4-beat bursts
-- * Checks HBURST is correctly encoded for 4-beat bursts (checked by tb_dma)
--
--
-- Detailed Test Description
-- -------------------------
-- 1. Check and initialise the relevant registers
-- 2. Transmit a long frame that just fills the buffer.
-- 3. Transmit a long frame that just overflows the buffer.
-- 4. Queue a short frame to check buffer is recovered
-- 5. Check the status and statistics registers and ensure that the 
--     above operations were handled properly.
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------


--******************************************************************************
-- 1. Check and initialise the relevant registers
--******************************************************************************
apbrd(100) 00 00000000  -- check reset value of network control register
apbwr      10 00020504  -- set the TX packet buffer RAM to FULL (bit 10), 4-beat
apbwr      00 00000008  -- enable transmit
apbrd      24 00000000  -- check interrupt status
apbwr      28 ffffffff  -- enable all interrupts
apbrd      24 00000000  -- check interrupt status
apbrd      30 00000000  -- check that all interrupts are now enabled
apbrd      04 00080000  -- check reset value of network config register
apbrd      08 00000006  -- check reset value of network status register
apbwr      04 00200009  -- 100Meg mode, jumbo frames enabled
apbrd      04 00200009  -- verify write to speed register..
apbrdf     20 00000000  -- check contents of the receive status register and trigger reception of frame



